# Rules for Fidelity "History for Account" exports (SPAXX).
# Expected columns: Run Date,Action,Symbol,Description,Type,Price ($),Quantity,
# Commission ($),Fees ($),Accrued Interest ($),Amount ($),Cash Balance ($),Settlement Date
#
# Fidelity's raw export has 2 blank lines then a header line before the
# data, and a legal-disclaimer footer after it — neither is valid CSV, so
# trim both before importing (keep the header line + data rows only).
# This rules file assumes that trim has already been done, i.e. the header
# is on line 1 — adjust `skip` below if you're feeding it the raw export.
#
# Usage:
#   hledger import csv/fidelity.csv --rules rules/fidelity.csv.rules -f ledger/2026.journal

skip 1
fields date, action, symbol, description, txntype, price, quantity, commission, fees, accruedinterest, amount, balance, settlementdate

date-format %m/%d/%Y

currency $

account1 assets:fidelity
balance %balance

# Dividends are real interest income.
if DIVIDEND RECEIVED
    account2 income:interest

# Reinvestment of that same dividend back into the money-market fund is a
# same-day wash with no net effect in our flat "SPAXX = cash" model — skip
# it rather than post a no-op transfer to itself.
if REINVESTMENT
    skip

# Chase autopay from this account (mirrors the Chase-side rule) — routed
# through the same clearing account so both sides net to zero.
if DIRECT DEBIT CHASE CREDIT
    account2 equity:transfers

# Incoming transfers default to capital contributions, since that's the
# common case. One known exception: the 2026-05-26 transfer is the tail
# end of the Bluevine account closure (Bluevine -> FirstBank -> Fidelity),
# already fully recorded by the Bluevine rules, so skip it here to avoid
# double-counting.
if %action TRANSFERRED FROM VS && %date 05/26/2026
    skip

if TRANSFERRED FROM VS
    account2 equity:member-capital
